@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Chicago v26.10.1 narrative projection facts (pack-side, RESOLUTIONS R3).
#
# These are graph facts, never template constants. Every string below is
# composed strictly from claims already admitted in the canonical graphs
# (goal.ttl / chicago.ttl / projections.ttl). No outcome is pre-judged and no
# standing is asserted here: all rendered standing remains UNKNOWN until a
# real receipt binds observed execution (RESOLUTIONS R8).
#
# Consumers: queries/executive.rq (narrative + failureRecovery + polarity),
# queries/machine.rq and queries/verification.rq (layer contract ids).

# --- Executive narrative (one node, R3 narrative schema) ---

chi:narrative-purchase-001
    a chi:Narrative ;
    rdfs:label "Chicago v26.10.1 executive narrative" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf chi:GC-XAAS-26.10.1-CHICAGO ;
    chi:narrativeFor chi:purchase-001 ;
    chi:audience "Executive seller audience (non-technical stakeholder); no repository mechanics are required for this narrative." ;
    chi:headline "XaaS v26.10.1 Chicago ecosystem demo: one exact Agentic Payments subject, projected across every ecosystem layer" ;
    chi:customerProblem "Requirement tracking, semantic admission, delegated capability, planning, runtime execution, process evidence, evidence standing and human projection usually live in different systems that each hold a different copy of the subject, so nobody can see one deal end to end without hand-stitching tools that were never designed to agree." ;
    chi:desiredOutcome "One exact Agentic Payments subject, urn:chicago:agentic-payment:purchase-001, is visible through sJira, semantic law, SA2A, planning, runtime, OCEL, process conformance, evidence standing and human projection without changing subject identity, and no projection, analysis or UI surface gains DO authority." ;
    chi:semanticPath "docs/sjira/v26.10.1/ goal graph (RDF source) -> ggen-marketplace chicago-xaas-surface-pack deterministic render -> XaaS consumer projection -> AshSurface operator/Chicago/seller views" .

# --- Layer contract ids (graph IRIs -> consumer contract slugs, RESOLUTIONS R2) ---

