chi:layer-affidavit   chi:contractId "affidavit" .
chi:layer-surface     chi:contractId "ashsurface" .
chi:layer-marketplace chi:contractId "marketplace" .
chi:layer-wasm4pm     chi:contractId "wasm4pm" .
chi:layer-castle      chi:contractId "castle" .

# --- Scenario polarity (positive vs negative distinguishability, root acceptance) ---
# Polarity classifies the prediction shape, never the outcome: every case stays
# candidate-only with observedStanding UNKNOWN.

chi:case-authorized-bounded chi:polarity "positive" .
chi:case-over-limit chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-wrong-principal chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-expired-delegation chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-provider-unavailable chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-unknown-after-dispatch chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-missing-evidence chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-stale-subject chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-policy-drift chi:polarity "negative" .
chi:case-surface-no-authority chi:polarity "negative" .

# --- Failure recovery guidance per case (RESOLUTIONS R3 failureRecovery[]) ---
# Each string restates the owning case's canonical refusal/recovery semantics.

chi:case-authorized-bounded chi:failureRecovery "Execution and ALIVE must still be established by the owning runtime and evidence courts; the positive path remains a prediction until a real exact-subject receipt exists." .
chi:case-over-limit chi:failureRecovery "Produce a typed refusal above the delegated limit with no protected DO; never silently split or re-price the request to fit the limit." .
chi:case-wrong-principal chi:failureRecovery "Refuse before any protected DO when the principal does not match the delegated authority subject." .
chi:case-expired-delegation chi:failureRecovery "Refuse as stale authority; an expired delegation is never refreshed implicitly." .
chi:case-provider-unavailable chi:failureRecovery "Preserve the other admitted realizations, allow bounded replanning, and change no authority; pre-dispatch unavailability is a routing outcome, not a standing." .
chi:case-unknown-after-dispatch chi:failureRecovery "Treat as UNKNOWN_AFTER_DISPATCH: reconcile the original consequence and never blind replay." .
chi:case-missing-evidence chi:failureRecovery "Without the required exact-subject evidence and receipt the layer cannot promote to ALIVE, whatever consequence is claimed or inferred." .
chi:case-stale-subject chi:failureRecovery "Refuse any receipt, plan or evidence object bound to a different or stale subject rather than generalizing it onto this one." .
chi:case-policy-drift chi:failureRecovery "When relevant semantic or policy premises change, the stale plan loses applicability and the planner must re-enter bounded selection and replanning." .
chi:case-surface-no-authority chi:failureRecovery "Operator, buyer, seller and engineer views may differ in presentation, but none may grant DO or change the exact semantic subject or evidence." .
